  "note": "Poses: the body frame's origin is the left imager's optical centre, which the datasheet names as the depth origin (section 4.8.1, \"the X-Y center of the left imager\"); the right imager sits one baseline along -y (the left imager is on the left looking out, section 3.6.1). Both optical axes are taken as parallel to body x (the rectified stereo geometry the depth output uses); the units' own extrinsics come from calibration. The D405 has no separate RGB camera: \"Left depth sensor provides RGB data to color ISP\" (Table 2-1 note 4, Table 3-20 note), so the RGB imager is the left imager (pose stated, the same optical centre); its colour FOV is Table 3-20's 84 x 58 x 92 (the stereo imagers' own table, 3-15, gives 90 x 64 x 98 for the 1280 x 800 sensor; Table 3-20 lists 84 x 58 x 92 beside 1280 x 800 active pixels and does not say which stream it is for, so a 1280 x 720 colour stream gets a FOV derived by a centred crop, labelled as such). The imagers have an IR-cut filter and there is no IR projector: a passive stereo camera (\"KPIs for D405, a passive camera, are measured using a textured target and typical ambient room light (~250 Lux)\", Table 4-15 note 4). Not stated by the maker: pixel size (no table gives it), lens distortion coefficients (the datasheet gives only \"Distortion <= 1.5%\"), the stereo matcher's subpixel accuracy. The lens model is therefore pinhole (a labelled assumption); calibrate a unit for its own K and D. The FOVs vary unit to unit by about +/-3 degrees (mechanical tolerance +/-5%, datasheet Table 3-49 note 3). max_range_m is the upper figure of the datasheet's \"Range\" feature line, \"Range 7 cm to 1 m (varies with lighting conditions)\" (depth.range_text); unlike the other D400 lines it does not say \"over\". Stream modes are the USB 3.1 Gen 1 tables; the USB 2.0 tables (fewer modes) are not entered. power_w is the datasheet's \"All Components\" power at its Max Operating Mode (section 7.4), not a measured average. The min-Z table gives \"-\" for 640x480 (m null). Sources disagree: the datasheet gives the depth FOV as H 84 / V 58 / D 92 at 20 cm (used), the store page \"87 x 58\"; the datasheet connector section is \"USB Peripheral Connector - Micro-B (D405)\" with a USB3 Micro-B receptacle, the store page lists \"USB-C 3.1 Gen 1\"; the store page gives \"Ideal Range 7 cm to 50 cm\", min-Z \"~7 cm @ 480p\" (the table's 70 mm at 848x480), depth accuracy \"<2% at 50 cm\" and RGB up to 1280 x 800 at 90 fps, where the datasheet's colour stream table stops at 1280 x 720. power_w is at the D405's Max Operating Mode, 848x480 @ 90 fps depth and colour (Table 7-10). Timing (read 2026-11-07): the datasheet's exposure table (Table 4-23, Depth Camera Controls) names the 400/410 and 430 modules, not this one, so no exposure range is entered (null); no readout time is stated for any imager (null); section 7.13 says the D405 does not support the hardware sync signal.",
